---
import ThemeToggle from "../../../../src/astro/ThemeToggle.astro";
import Shell from "../../../../src/astro/v2/Shell.astro";
import Header from "../../../../src/astro/v2/Header.astro";
import ContextNav from "../../../../src/astro/v2/ContextNav.astro";
import Sidebar from "../../../../src/astro/v2/Sidebar.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const basePath = base.endsWith("/") ? base : `${base}/`;
const worldAroundLab = `${basePath}v2/world/around/`;

const worldSidebar = [
  { label: "Feed", items: [
    { href: "#world", label: "All transmissions", current: true, badge: 24 },
    { href: worldAroundLab, label: "Around Hara", badge: 42 },
    { href: "#world", label: "Following", badge: 8 },
    { href: "#world", label: "Announcements", badge: 3 }
  ] },
  { label: "Directory", items: [
    { href: "#world", label: "People" },
    { href: "#world", label: "Agents" },
    { href: worldAroundLab, label: "Sources" }
  ] }
];
---
<section class="v2-lab-section" id="world">
  <header class="v2-lab-section-head">
    <div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Layout 05 · Community publication</p><h2>World</h2></div>
    <p>An editorial surface inside the same fleet language. Paper-like panels and compact directories keep it humane; native posts, external signals, source registration, and feed management remain explicit and attributable.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="v2-lab-canvas" data-layout="world">
    <Shell embedded={true} sidebar={true} aside={true} mainId="world-content">
      <Header slot="header" section="World" nav={[
        { href: "#www", label: "Home" },
        { href: "#world", label: "World", current: true },
        { href: "#specs", label: "Specs" },
        { href: "#docs", label: "Packages" },
        { href: "#world", label: "Identity" }
      ]}>
        <button class="hara-v2-icon-button" aria-label="Account">◎</button>
        <ThemeToggle />
      </Header>
      <ContextNav slot="context" items={[
        { href: "#world", label: "Feed", current: true },
        { href: worldAroundLab, label: "Around Hara" },
        { href: "#world", label: "People" },
        { href: "#world", label: "Agents" },
        { href: worldAroundLab, label: "Sources" }
      ]}>
        <a class="hara-v2-button" href={worldAroundLab}>Add a source</a>
        <a class="hara-v2-button" data-variant="primary" href={worldAroundLab}>Explore signals ↗</a>
      </ContextNav>
      <Sidebar slot="sidebar" title="Community signal" groups={worldSidebar}>
        <span>Updated from 17 community feeds and 26 external sources.</span>
      </Sidebar>

      <div class="hara-v2-row" data-spread="true">
        <div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Community transmission</p><h1 class="v2-lab-docs-title">Hara World</h1></div>
        <span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="success">43 sources online</span>
      </div>
      <div class="v2-lab-world-grid">
        <div class="hara-v2-feed">
          <article class="hara-v2-story"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">HZ</div><div><h3>Typed schemas are becoming ordinary Hara values</h3><p>A field note on moving validation from metadata into the language's portable data model.</p><div class="hara-v2-story-meta"><span>Chris Zheng</span><span>std.typed</span><span>6 min</span></div></div><time>07:12</time></article>
          <article class="hara-v2-story"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">Y</div><div><div class="hara-v2-row"><span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="signal">External signal · Hacker News</span><span class="hara-v2-badge">Top 6% today</span></div><h3>Why Hara's LiveSession boundary reads more like a protocol</h3><p>Around Hara resolved this discussion to LiveSession, hara-wasm-core, and the canonical merged implementation.</p><div class="hara-v2-story-meta"><span>original platform retained</span><span>8-signal cluster</span><span>14 World comments</span></div></div><time>18 min</time></article>
          <article class="hara-v2-story"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">AG</div><div><h3>Agent registry field report: first signed capability record</h3><p>A registered agent publishes a narrow command surface and a verifiable revision.</p><div class="hara-v2-story-meta"><span>World Relay</span><span>agents</span><span>4 min</span></div></div><time>06:44</time></article>
          <article class="hara-v2-story"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">HB</div><div><h3>Hoplite raw interfaces now cover more of the host</h3><p>What moves out of Host/call when the web server becomes a first-class Hara surface.</p><div class="hara-v2-story-meta"><span>Hoplite</span><span>web</span><span>8 min</span></div></div><time>Yesterday</time></article>
        </div>
        <div class="v2-lab-world-side">
          <section class="v2-lab-lesson"><span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="signal">Around Hara</span><h3>Five sources, one story</h3><p>Explore attributed signals from X, Reddit, Hacker News, Substack, and GitHub without flattening unlike engagement metrics.</p><a href={worldAroundLab}>Open signal radar →</a></section>
          <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Who is using Hara</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body"><div class="hara-v2-profile-list"><article class="hara-v2-profile"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">GW</div><div><b>Greenways</b><p>Publishing tools and verifiable worlds.</p></div></article><article class="hara-v2-profile"><div class="hara-v2-avatar">HP</div><div><b>Hoplite</b><p>Programmable web services.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div slot="aside" class="v2-lab-inspector-stack">
        <section class="hara-v2-panel" data-sketch="true"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Signal watch</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body"><dl><div><dt>Native posts</dt><dd>12</dd></div><div><dt>External matches</dt><dd>42</dd></div><div><dt>Story clusters</dt><dd>5</dd></div><div><dt>Needs review</dt><dd>3</dd></div></dl></div></section>
        <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Around Hara</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body"><p>External platforms own their posts. World owns the Hara-specific connections, clips, local discussion, and accountable relay policy around them.</p><div class="hara-v2-stack"><a class="hara-v2-button" data-variant="primary" href={worldAroundLab}>Explore feed</a><a class="hara-v2-button" href={`${worldAroundLab}#submit`}>Submit source</a><a class="hara-v2-button" href={`${worldAroundLab}#relay`}>Review Hara Relay</a></div></div></section>
      </div>
    </Shell>
  </div>
  <div class="v2-lab-notes">
    <article><b>Mixed, not muddled</b><p>Native posts, canonical updates, external signals, and user-authored clips use distinct labels inside one reading surface.</p></article>
    <article><b>Source-relative ranking</b><p>X likes, Reddit votes, and Hacker News points remain source facts; percentile and velocity make comparison explainable.</p></article>
    <article><b>Accountable commands</b><p>Submit, clip, discuss, and relay actions stay visible without turning the front page into an automation dashboard.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
